#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171733 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fffe685-2f1e-5f0c-ab6a-db5786f40143" :knowledge-point/title "Disproving Parity and Divisibility Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "753bc7ba-2d9a-598a-8b39-19d4292b6cdc" :question/math-academy-id "e-13338" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n> $2 \\mid n^2-3$ for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n$\\forall n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\mid n^2-3$.\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\neg \\big(\\forall n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\mid n^2-3\\big) \\: \\equiv \\: \\exists n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\not\\mid n^2-3\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\n> To disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that\n> $2 \\not\\mid n^2-3$.\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=0$ suffices:\n\n> Notice that by substituting $n=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n> $n^{2} - 3|= (0)^{2} - 3; =-3$\n> which is not divisible by $2$.\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\n> So, $n=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171736 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171929 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ffc9f1-9524-50c2-8ae8-e01236f453b4" :knowledge-point/title "Stating Counterexample Conditions"}] :question/id #uuid "525511f3-67d1-56e3-93ab-acd4e9801e96" :question/math-academy-id "e-13352" :question/problem "What would be a counterexample for the following false statement?\n\n> $7n-2$ is even for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n7n - 2\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true.\n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true.\n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n7n - 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n> A counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that $7n-2$ is odd."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171737 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44e48ea1-2219-5954-8101-def7c9c2be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Disproving Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "331f2d85-cde0-5d83-abce-910d845845f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-13353" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n> $3q^2-2 \\gt 0$ for any $q \\in \\mathbb{Q}$." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n$\\forall q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\gt 0$.\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\neg \\big(\\forall q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\gt 0 \\big) \\: \\equiv \\: \\exists q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\n> To disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a rational number $q$ such that\n> $3q^2-2 \\leq 0$.\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $q=0$ suffices:\n\n> By substituting $q=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n> $3q^{2} - 2|= 3(0)^{2} - 2; =-2; \\le 0$.\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\n> So, $q=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171929 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ffc9f1-9524-50c2-8ae8-e01236f453b4" :knowledge-point/title "Stating Counterexample Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce010843-c0d5-5cfc-8836-d64dc0f58d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169687} {:answer/id #uuid "de25818a-8d5c-56c2-94a4-9b176a3dbeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169688} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2ab8d0-7d7a-52de-a0b0-abcbb26b0e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169689} {:answer/id #uuid "0b4c3f32-b02a-56f3-b868-86f1b66eae82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169690}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbe8847-8044-53e4-9ee9-a2a1a29e84bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d675176d-cc53-5b07-a06e-6126d2ef217b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n^{2} - 6n + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169692} {:answer/id #uuid "5352beef-7695-518a-9d19-b7691ed5c267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169693}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9940dd2a-b5e5-5288-859b-655d21ecb420" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25d125b-fe44-536b-be8d-45a74a2f476f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169695} {:answer/id #uuid "27e13f7e-9c6a-5dbb-9436-dc22ce303787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169696} {:answer/id #uuid "766d5e9f-f89e-512d-ba9e-b500c75b9a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169697}] :answer-field/id #uuid "25813b83-7dca-5d22-bff4-dd61e7c8247c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169694}] :question/id #uuid "22d71c4d-b3cd-5679-8624-1ff129268ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-185001" :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\n> $n^{2} - 6n + 8 \\ge 0$ for any $n ∈ N$.\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that\n$n^{2} - 6n + 8$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}"}]}
